course: dictionary
lesson: 4045
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One short word can have several meanings. Gen is a good example. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants, so look for context clues first.
explain: «Gen Z» and «Gen Alpha» are names for groups of people born around the same time, because gen is short for generation. In «Gen 1:1», gen is short for Genesis, the first book of the Bible, so that is a different meaning again.
explain: Informal talk adds more meanings. «I'm gen tired» means genuinely, like saying honestly or for real. «Give me the gen» means give me the information or the facts, and that is an old-fashioned informal use in Britain.
explain: Check the clues. A year, a group of people, a Bible reference or a rank before a name each points to one meaning. Then use the swap test: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Gen is short for generation, a group of people born around the same time.
fact: «Gen Z» and «Gen Alpha» are names for two such groups.
fact: «I'm gen tired» means I'm genuinely tired. Here gen is an adverb.
fact: «Give me the gen» means give me the information or the facts. This is an informal, old-fashioned use in Britain.
fact: «Gen.» is a short form of General, as in «Gen. Washington». «Gen 1:1» is the first verse of Genesis.
exercise: «Gen Z» and «Gen Alpha» are groups of people born around the same time. What does gen stand for? | Genesis | *Generation | General | Genuine
exercise: Priya says, «I'm gen tired after the match.» What does gen mean here? | The information about the match | Generation, a group of people | *Genuinely, meaning really | A general in the army
exercise: In «Gen 1:1», what does Gen stand for? | Genuinely, for real | *Genesis, the first book of the Bible | General, the army rank | Generation, a group of people
test: Tom asks, «Give me the gen on the trip.» What does the gen mean? | *The information or facts about the trip | Genuine fun | A group of people born on the same day | A general from the army
test: In «Gen. Washington led the army», what does Gen. mean? | *General, a rank in the army | Genuinely | Generation | Genesis
exam: Which sentence uses gen to mean genuinely? | The gen of the trip was clear | Gen Alpha is a group born around the same time | The new console is the next-gen version | *I'm gen sorry I was late
